From: freiheit93 board bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx93-11x11-frdm: disable lpuart5 hw flow control

The onboard NXP IW612 WiFi/BT combo chip's Bluetooth function is
attached to lpuart5. Mainline's uart-has-rtscts on this node causes
the LPUART peripheral to gate outgoing HCI commands on the chip's CTS
line; the chip never actually receives them on this board revision,
so every HCI command (starting with HCI_Reset, opcode 0x0c03) times
out with -110 even though the driver-level TX path reports success
(confirmed via btmon: command sent, no response ever, including well
after boot with WLAN fully initialized and the combo firmware's own
"boot sign" already detected as present).

NXP's own downstream reference DTS for the physically identical
board (meta-imx-frdm, imx93-11x11-frdm basic support patch) does not
set uart-has-rtscts on this node at all. Drop it to match.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific hardware workaround,
not yet root-caused at the electrical level; needs confirmation
before submitting upstream]

Signed-off-by: freiheit93 board bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-11x11-frdm.dts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-11x11-frdm.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-11x11-frdm.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-11x11-frdm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-11x11-frdm.dts
@@ -387,8 +387,6 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	status = "okay";

-	uart-has-rtscts;
-
 	bluetooth {
 		compatible = "nxp,88w8987-bt";
 		device-wakeup-gpios = <&pcal6408 3 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
--
2.43.0
